3. Evolution vs Moral Devolution

Modern Science
	•	Biological evolution → complexity increases
	•	No moral or spiritual metric
	•	Time is value-neutral

Yuga System
	•	Physical form may persist
	•	Dharma declines
	•	Consciousness degrades across Yugas

This means:
	•	Scientific progress can increase
	•	Ethical and spiritual capacity can still decline

These views are not contradictory—they operate on different axes.

⸻

4. Long Time Spans Are Scientifically Acceptable

Modern science already accepts:
	•	Stellar lifetimes in billions of years
	•	Galactic cycles in trillions of years
	•	Unknown pre-Big-Bang conditions

Therefore, the objection to Yuga durations is philosophical, not scientific.

⸻

5. Why Ancient Texts Used Vast Numbers
	•	Oral traditions required precise ratios
	•	Decimal repetition improves memorability
	•	Large numbers reflect cosmic—not human—reference frames

The base number 432,000 appears repeatedly because it is:
	•	Divisible
	•	Cyclical
	•	Structurally scalable

⸻

Scientific Summary
	•	Science answers how matter behaves
	•	Sanātana Dharma answers how order decays
	•	Both accept vast cosmic time
	•	They differ in purpose, not scale


